# sirius: the Image4 ignition sysctl parks the exec'd image (2026-10-28 15:22 capture)
#
# Kernel 0ff05f7f7fec75a54b5d6071c452bc6ce19f5d527eefb5d09a415e58742ed7e4 (syscall limit raised
# from 24 to 256 and the sysctl MIB traced); payload-full.img sha256 8cd27069...; same union and
# trust-cache arguments as the 14:50 boot. Raw capture: .scratch/console-sysctl-20261028-1522.log.
#
# What it shows: the "24 launchd syscalls" of the earlier captures were the trace's cap, not a
# stop. The exec'd dyld gets through kern.bootargs (MIB 1.149) and then calls sysctl on
# security.mac.img4.ignition_blob (MIB 101.100.118.100). It never returns: the pid 1 thread is
# inside sysctl_root/sysctl with 31 syscalls entered and 30 returned, and its saved user PC is
# the instruction after dyld's __sysctl svc. The Image4 handler (AppleImage4 kext) waits without
# a timeout for an IOAESAccelerator service; SDM710 publishes none, so libignition parks before
# it can publish the ignition blob. Enabling the software AES personality is the next build.
#
